One of three problems in [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) ([the split](/kb/incidents/4471-split)).
Ticket: [#1](https://github.com/vedhav/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} only="parser" what={{ parser: 'The shared parser read every date month first.' }} />

## What happened

All 11 tenants in #4471 write the day first. The shared parser read every date month first, so
day and month swapped wherever both are 12 or less:

> Booked for 2 March. The invite says 3 February.
>
> The reminder for 12 January arrived for 1 December.

It came in through every channel: the app, email, and `booking-v2` forms, whose hint
(`DD/MM/YYYY`) matches what the tenant's people type.

## How to recognise it

A day-first tenant, a date with day and month swapped, and not a `booking-v3` form (that is
[hint](/kb/incidents/4471-hint)).

## State

Fixed by engineering: *fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales*. #4471 closed 5 October. A swap
reported after that date is a regression of this fix, not a new ticket for #4471.

